==Personal life==
In 1985, at age 18, she married and moved to [[Joliet, Illinois]] with her first husband. They were divorced two years later.<ref name="Website-1" /> Demuth married Nick Demuth in 1991.<ref>{{Cite web |title= What to know about Lisa Demuth, Minnesota's GOP nominee for governor |url= https://www.startribune.com/what-to-know-about-lisa-demuth-minnesotas-gop-nominee-for-governor/601877978 |website=The Minnesota Star Tribune}}</ref> They reside in [[Cold Spring, Minnesota]], and have four children.<ref name= "lpp" /> All their children were on campus when a gunman killed two students in the [[2003 Rocori High School shooting]].<ref>{{Cite news |last= Chapman |first= Reg |date= May 17, 2025 |title= Minnesota House Speaker Lisa Demuth's daughter criticizes her handling of gun control bill |url= https://www.cbsnews.com/minnesota/news/minnesota-house-speaker-lisa-demuth-daughter-gun-reform/ |access-date= May 17, 2025 |work= [[CBS Minnesota]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last= Orenstein |first= Walker |date= April 8, 2026 |title= How a 2003 school shooting is influencing the Minnesota House speaker's response to Annunciation |url= https://www.startribune.com/how-a-2003-school-shooting-is-influencing-the-minnesota-house-speakers-response-to-annunciation/601658449 |access-date= April 8, 2026 |work= [[Star Tribune]]}}</ref> Demuth co-owns and manages commercial property with her husband.<ref name="tnl_20181019" /><ref name="News-1" />

She is a member of an [[Assemblies of God USA|Assemblies of God]] Pentecostal congregation in [[Cold Spring, Minnesota|Cold Spring]] and has described her faith as central to her life.<ref name="Website-1" />

